{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.DescartesBraidStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.DescartesBraidStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dic3_divides_s5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dic3_divides_s5","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L94-L96","doc":"Dic₃ order divides S₅ order: 12 | 120. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.thirty_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.thirty_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L88-L92","doc":"The invertibility requirement: 30 must be invertible in the base ring.\n30 = 2 · 3 · 5, which is |S₅| / |Dic₃| · (correction factors).\nThis ensures the representation theory works integrally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.colour_sectors_account_for_eighteen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.colour_sectors_account_for_eighteen","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L79-L86","doc":"The colour sectors account for 18 elements of S₅: `colourSectorCount`\ncopies of S₃, each of order `3! = 6`.  (This is the count the section\ndocstring above records; the copies are subgroups, so they are not\ndisjoint as sets.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.colourSectorCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.colourSectorCount","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L66-L77","doc":"The number of colour sectors — copies of S₃ inside S₅, one per colour\n(red, green, blue).  A **named constant** of the model, not a theorem.\n\nReplaced `theorem colour_sector_count : (3 : ℕ) = 3 := rfl`\n(2026-08-21; vacuity ledger, `reflexive-tautology-ascribed-literal`).\nThat statement held whatever the number of colour sectors happened to\nbe — no definition of the sector set appeared in it, so nothing tied\nthe `3` to the corpus.  Per Strict Lean Discipline §8 a claim with no\nfalsifiable content is notation, so it is a `def`; the one falsifiable\nthing its docstring asserted is stated below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.s5_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.s5_order","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L62-L64","doc":"S₅ has order 120. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.s3_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.s3_order","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L56-L60","doc":"S₃ has order 6, and three disjoint copies inside S₅ account for\n3 × 6 = 18 elements (as subgroups, they are not disjoint as sets,\nbut the corollary states they correspond to the three colour sectors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dic3_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dic3_order","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The binary dihedral group Dic₃ has order 4n for n = 3, i.e. 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.kernel_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.kernel_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Faithfulness: |ker ρ₃| = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.kernelOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.kernelOrder","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The representation is faithful: kernel is trivial.\nEncoded as: the kernel order is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.aut_order_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.aut_order_eq","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L45-L45","doc":"|S₅| = 120. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.autOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.autOrder","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The order of the symmetric group S₅ = Aut(Σ₄). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.image_order_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.image_order_eq","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The image order is 12 (|Dic₃| = 4 · 3 = 12). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.imageOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.imageOrder","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Order of the binary dihedral image Dic₃ ⊂ SU(2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.strands_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.strands_eq","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Number of strands is 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.numStrands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.numStrands","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The tensor power (number of strands in the braid group). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.dimV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.dimV","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Dimension of the fundamental representation V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DescartesBraidStructure","kind":"structure","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-braid-structure.lean#L20-L50","doc":"**Descartes braid structure**: packages the algebraic data arising from\nthe braiding on a Descartes universe.\n\nGiven a Descartes universe (C, A, τ) with C = Rep(SU_q(2)):\n1. The braiding induces ρ₃ : B₃ → Aut_C(V^⊗3)\n2. The image under the fibre functor τ is Dic₃ ⊂ SU(2), order 12\n3. The composite B₃ → Dic₃ ↠ S₃ yields three copies of S₃ ⊂ S₅\n4. The structure is defined over any ring R with 30 ∈ R×\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{cor:descartes-braid-structure}`\nRef: [turaev2010] https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110218145 ","signatureChunk":0}]}